# @spectral/gen_prism/mcp_session — the MCP-session species of the
# @spectral/gen_prism family: a per-session gen_prism specialisation
# whose observable state IS an accumulated @spec crystal in
# @mirror/store, addressed by a content-addressed session ref, mutated
# by a read-head-crystal → apply-mq-tick → write-new-crystal →
# CAS-advance-ref loop. M1 TICK 1 landing per Reed's RED tick
# `e8378ca` (bootstrap/tests/spectral_gen_prism_mcp_session_shard.rs)
# and per collapse spec `docs/specs/mcp-spec-song-collapse.md` §3.5
# (MCP-as-state-machine narrative), §3.6 (statelessness at process /
# statefulness at store), §10.1 (M1 charter), §11.6.3 (session
# persistence agentic value-add).
#
# === Substrate-canonical placement rationale ===
#
# This species lives at `shards/spectral/gen_prism/mcp_session.mirror`
# — declaring `@spectral/gen_prism/mcp_session` under the
# @spectral/gen_prism family root — NOT at
# `shards/mirror/runtime/mcp_session.mirror` (the collapse spec §3.5
# grammar name). Rationale per Taut scout finding + per
# `[[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]`: the gen_prism family
# ALREADY lives at @spectral (per `shards/spectral/gen_prism.mirror`
# `227c0e0`-era landing); the runtime specialisation cascade is
# @spectral's cascade; MCP session IS a gen_prism specialisation
# (per collapse spec §9.3 candidate "MCP session IS gen_prism"), so
# it lives where the gen_prism family lives. The alternative
# @mirror/runtime placement would require inventing a parallel
# runtime family root that the substrate does not carry. The
# substrate-canonical location wins; the spec grammar name is
# superseded by structural placement (per Alex 2026-07-01 legibility-
# over-foundation discipline generalised to placement).
#
# === Species contract: gen_prism specialised for MCP JSON-RPC wire ===
#
# Per `shards/spectral/gen_prism.mirror` §"State surface — shard_ref"
# and §"Tool surface — the five-op block": every gen_prism carries
# three surfaces — identity (uuid_spectral), state (shard_ref into
# @mirror/store), tool surface (the five-op block IS the wire
# protocol). This species specialises each surface for MCP:
#
#   - identity: `uuid_spectral` — the session identifier; ACTIVE 48
#     bits route the session in the substrate's spectral manifold
#     (Fate reads through this for session-scoped routing); DARK 80
#     bits identify the session content-addressably for the ref
#     lookup and cross-daemon-restart persistence.
#   - state: `shard_ref` — the head crystal of the accumulated @spec
#     the session has been building. State lives in @mirror/store;
#     the Rust MCP handler at `bootstrap/src/mcp.rs` holds ONLY the
#     session-uuid, NEVER the accumulated @spec content itself.
#   - tool surface: the five-op block from @spectral/gen_prism,
#     specialised as the mq (mirror query language, per
#     `boot/std/code/mq.mirror`) wire vocabulary — MCP JSON-RPC
#     requests translate directly to mq queries; each request IS
#     one tick of the session's mq trajectory.
#
# === Session ref discipline — refs/gen_prism/mcp/<session-uuid> ===
#
# Per collapse spec §3.6: the session ref is a content-addressed
# pointer at `refs/gen_prism/mcp/<session-uuid>` inside @mirror/store,
# pointing at the head crystal of the accumulated @spec. The ref
# pattern is:
#
#   refs/gen_prism/mcp/<session-uuid>  →  <crystal-oid>
#
# where <session-uuid> is the session's `uuid_spectral` and
# <crystal-oid> is the BLAKE3-content-address of the head @spec
# crystal.
#
# The ref is stable across process restarts because it lives in
# @mirror/store (git-backed at the M6 TICK 1 Apache-2.0 rock-solid
# floor per `884f433`). A daemon restart re-reads the ref by
# session-uuid; the accumulated @spec content is intact because
# every intermediate crystal is content-addressed in the store's
# DAG. This IS the M6 floor's first-order capability specialised
# at MCP altitude — the mcp_session species is the first substrate
# consumer of Recognition #43 (mirror IS content-addressed build
# system) at a runtime-facing altitude.
#
# The CAS (compare-and-swap) advance semantic is the substrate's
# session-mutation primitive: the tick body reads the ref's
# current head, computes the new crystal, and CAS-advances the ref
# from old-head to new-head. Concurrent-request contention is
# resolved at the ref-advance edge (git-ref-style; the losing tick
# retries).
#
# === State-lives-in-@mirror/store discipline ===
#
# Per collapse spec §3.6: MCP is STATELESS AT THE PROCESS LAYER
# BECAUSE it is STATEFUL AT THE STORE LAYER. This inversion IS the
# species's load-bearing discipline. The Rust MCP handler
# (`bootstrap/src/mcp.rs`) never holds session state; every
# observable session transition is a content-addressed crystal
# in @mirror/store. Consequences:
#
#   - the accumulated @spec IS a chain of crystals in the store's
#     DAG; each mq query produces one new crystal linked to its
#     predecessor;
#   - the query trajectory IS the crystal ancestor chain — replay
#     and audit come for free from the store's DAG structure;
#   - the Hilbert dimension of the accumulated recognitions IS the
#     ancestor-chain depth (per Recognition #51 mirror-as-expanding-
#     Hilbert-space; each mq query lifts the dimension by one);
#   - session persistence across daemon restart IS free (no
#     serialization; the store IS the serialization);
#   - concurrent read-only queries never conflict (crystals are
#     immutable-under-hash per @mirror/store Recognition #43);
#   - write conflicts resolve at ref-advance-by-CAS (git-ref
#     semantic).
#
# The species is thus the first-order consumer that proves the M6
# TICK 1 Apache-2.0 rock-solid floor. If any of these consequences
# fail to hold, the floor is wrong. If they all hold, the floor
# stands ratified — not analytically, but empirically through
# consumer discharge.
#
# === Tick semantics — read / apply mq / write / CAS-advance ===
#
# Per collapse spec §3.6 + §10.1: each MCP request drives one tick
# of the session's state machine. The tick's four phases:
#
#   1. READ. Look up `refs/gen_prism/mcp/<session-uuid>` in
#      @mirror/store; resolve to the head crystal-oid; read the
#      crystal's content into the tick body as the input @spec.
#   2. APPLY. Decode the MCP JSON-RPC request as an mq query
#      (per `boot/std/code/mq.mirror`); apply the query against
#      the input @spec; produce the output @spec + the response
#      payload.
#   3. WRITE. Content-address the output @spec; write the new
#      crystal to @mirror/store; get back the new-head crystal-oid.
#   4. CAS-ADVANCE. Compare-and-swap the session ref from
#      old-head-oid → new-head-oid. On success, emit the response;
#      on conflict, retry from step 1 (contention resolves at the
#      ref-advance edge).
#
# The tick IS the substrate-decl of the MCP session's mutation
# primitive. Rust wiring lands in a follow-on M1 tick; this shard
# declares the vocabulary the wiring will consume.
#
# === Tool surface — mq five-op wire specialised for JSON-RPC ===
#
# Per @spectral/gen_prism §"Tool surface — the five-op block": the
# five operations at runtime altitude specialise as follows for MCP:
#
#   focus @ mcp    project the head crystal's λ₀ eigenvalue — the
#                  canonical observable state of the session (what
#                  IS the session, right now, in one reading?).
#   project @ mcp  filter the head @spec to the caller-relevant
#                  subspace — the JSON-RPC response is an mq
#                  projection of the accumulated @spec through the
#                  request's field mask.
#   split @ mcp    orthogonal decomposition — split the accumulated
#                  @spec into constituent recognitions / candidates /
#                  ratifications (matches the spec DAG's edge
#                  classes).
#   shift @ mcp    basis transformation — same content, different
#                  altitude (e.g. render the accumulated @spec at
#                  the @io/oci altitude for a container-runnable
#                  view of the session).
#   settle @ mcp   measurement collapse — the session's settle_on
#                  ratifies the accumulated @spec and (per collapse
#                  spec §3.3) mirror kintsugi @spec spawns @song;
#                  the session enters its closure state.
#
# The tool surface IS the wire protocol (per @spectral/gen_prism
# discipline: external callers speak through the five-op surface;
# there is no out-of-band API). For MCP specifically, the wire IS
# JSON-RPC 2.0 (per collapse spec §3.5); each JSON-RPC method
# dispatches to one of the five ops through the mq query surface.
#
# === Accumulator discipline — session builds @spec across queries ===
#
# Per collapse spec §3.2: each mq query IS one substrate-pull
# dimension expansion. The session ACCUMULATES an @spec across
# queries — the head crystal at any tick carries the composed
# result of every prior query in the session. After N queries, the
# session's head crystal IS a partial @spec with N recognition-
# equivalent dimensions. When settle_on ratifies (per spec §3.3),
# mirror kintsugi @spec spawns @song and the accumulated content
# crystallises out of the session into the persistent @spec DAG.
#
# The accumulator discipline distinguishes MCP-session gen_prism
# from stateless RPC:
#
#   - stateless RPC: each request/reply is independent; no cross-
#     request accumulation;
#   - MCP session: each request advances the session's head crystal;
#     the accumulated @spec grows monotonically until settle_on
#     ratifies or the session closes without ratification (in which
#     case the accumulated intermediate crystals remain in the
#     store's DAG as a query trajectory but are not lifted to a
#     ratified @spec).
#
# The accumulator IS the substrate's answer to spec §3.2's "each
# mq query = one substrate-pull dimension expansion": dimension
# expansion happens at the session level; the accumulated @spec
# IS the Hilbert-space state carrying the session's recognitions.
#
# === Session persistence across daemon restart (§11.6.3) ===
#
# Per collapse spec §11.6.3: session persistence IS an agentic
# value-add of the MCP-as-gen_prism collapse. Because the session
# state lives in @mirror/store (not in-process), a daemon restart
# does not lose the accumulated @spec. The client re-connects with
# the same session-uuid; the daemon reads the head crystal from
# `refs/gen_prism/mcp/<session-uuid>` and resumes tick from the
# restored head. The client experiences no session interruption
# other than transport-layer reconnect.
#
# This survives:
#   - daemon crash + supervised restart (per @spectral/supervisor);
#   - deliberate daemon rollout (SIGTERM + fresh spawn);
#   - process boundary crossings (client reconnect to a different
#     daemon instance in a supervised cluster reads the same ref);
#   - machine reboot (the store's git-backed persistence survives).
#
# The persistence IS a first-order consequence of the state-lives-
# in-@mirror/store discipline. NOT an extra feature; the natural
# consequence of naming state properly.
#
# === Query trajectory replay + audit via ancestor chain ===
#
# Per collapse spec §6.4: the session's ancestor chain — the DAG
# path from the current head crystal back through every prior mq
# query's crystal — IS the query trajectory. Replay reconstructs
# any historical session state by walking the chain back to the
# desired ancestor; audit reads the chain to explain WHY the
# session's current head has the content it does. This composes
# with the M6 floor's provenance-chain value-add at MCP altitude:
#
#   - replay: any prior head crystal can be re-materialised as the
#     session state; the tick body is deterministic under the
#     store's content-addressed reads;
#   - audit: the ancestor chain names every mq query the session
#     applied, in order; the audit reader can reconstruct the
#     dialogue that produced the accumulated @spec;
#   - branching: alternative timelines (e.g. what would this
#     session's @spec look like if the third query had been
#     different?) fork off any ancestor; the DAG carries multiple
#     heads without contention because crystals are immutable-
#     under-hash.
#
# The query trajectory IS thus the audit trail. NOT a separate
# logging system; the substrate's DAG structure carries it by
# construction.
#
# === Prior art anchors — BEAM gen_server, nix-daemon, git ref advance ===
#
# The species inherits its ancestor recognition from three
# canonical prior-art traditions:
#
#   - BEAM gen_server / OTP (Ericsson 1986; Erlang/OTP standard
#     library since Erlang 5.0, 2000): the canonical stateful-
#     process-with-typed-message-surface pattern; each gen_server
#     handles messages in an isolated process with private state;
#     supervisors own the lifecycle. `@spectral/gen_prism` IS
#     the substrate's gen_server analogue (per gen_prism family
#     root docblock); this species specialises the analogue for
#     MCP JSON-RPC-driven session state.
#
#   - nix-daemon (NixOS 2005+; C++/Nix): the persistent-session-
#     via-socket-plus-store pattern. The nix-daemon holds no
#     build state itself; every build product is content-
#     addressed in the Nix store; the daemon is a thin dispatcher
#     that reads and writes the store on behalf of clients. Session
#     resumption across restart works because the store IS the
#     state. Dolstra 2006 (thesis) grounds the content-addressed
#     build system discipline that Recognition #43 lifted to
#     substrate altitude at M6 TICK 1.
#
#   - git ref advance-by-CAS (Torvalds 2005; git core): the CAS
#     ref-advance semantic. `git update-ref --create-reflog
#     <ref> <new> <old>` atomically advances the ref only if the
#     current value equals <old>; concurrent writes to the same
#     ref conflict at this edge and one loses. The MCP session
#     tick's step 4 IS this pattern specialised for
#     `refs/gen_prism/mcp/<session-uuid>` inside @mirror/store.
#
# All three prior-art traditions carry the same structural
# insight: STATE LIVES IN THE STORE, NOT IN THE PROCESS. The
# substrate lifts this to the mcp_session species by construction.
#
# === Recognition binding ===
#
# This species is a first-order consumer of Recognition #43
# (`[[architecture-mirror-as-content-addressed-build-system]]`;
# LANDED at M6 TICK 1 `884f433`). Every property Recognition #43
# names — content-addressed storage, immutable-under-hash keys,
# provenance-chain audit, session persistence via store — is
# consumed here at MCP altitude. If Recognition #43 stands, this
# species discharges cleanly. If any property of Recognition #43
# fails empirically at this consumer, the recognition needs
# refinement. The species IS thus the floor's first empirical
# proof at a runtime-facing altitude.
#
# Sub-recognition candidate flagged (NOT numbered): "MCP session
# IS gen_prism" per collapse spec §9.3. The recognition would say:
# the MCP JSON-RPC session concept and the @spectral/gen_prism
# worker-with-typed-surface concept are the SAME structural
# object viewed from different altitudes (protocol altitude vs
# runtime altitude). Promotion criterion pending Seam adjudication.
#
# === Circular-reflexive self-audit ===
#
# Per `[[architecture-candidate-recognition-111-third-as-family-root]]`
# marker discipline: the species-decl MUST survive the discipline
# it declares. Each of this shard's own recognitions:
#
#   - state lives in @mirror/store: this shard's authored content
#     lives at shards/spectral/gen_prism/mcp_session.mirror inside
#     the mirror repo, which IS the @mirror/store git-backed floor.
#     Discipline: pass.
#   - content-addressed identity: the shard's blob has a BLAKE3
#     content address at write; the gen_prism species named here
#     is content-addressable by its declaration OID. Discipline:
#     pass.
#   - tick semantics: the substrate-decl IS the specification;
#     downstream ticks read this shard, apply mq queries to derive
#     the Rust wiring, produce new shards; the meta-loop IS the
#     tick semantic applied to the substrate's own evolution.
#     Discipline: pass.
#
# Self-audit verdict: `both_survive`.
#
# === Interpretation B discipline ===
#
# Per Seam Phase D pre-review of the arc and per sibling species
# precedent (`shards/song/voice.mirror` `d5ea3f8`-era landing):
# Interpretation B canonical. Narrative-docblock ABOVE `---`;
# `in @` clauses BELOW. The seam is exactly one line at column 0
# below.
