in @prism
in @glass
in @meta
in @spectral
in @uuid/spectral
in @mirror/store

# ============================================================
# §1 The five-op tool surface at MCP session altitude
# ============================================================

# === glass @spectral/gen_prism/mcp_session — species declaration ===
#
# Per @spectral/gen_prism family root: `glass` is the substrate
# keyword for gen_prism-species specialisations (NOT a new keyword;
# per recognition #46 path-syntax property and per
# `shards/spectral.mirror`'s depth->=1 discipline).
#
# The five ops specialise at MCP altitude per family-root discipline
# (see docblock §"Tool surface — mq five-op wire specialised for
# JSON-RPC" above). The wire protocol IS JSON-RPC 2.0 dispatching
# through mq queries; external MCP clients speak to the session
# through this surface exclusively.
glass @spectral/gen_prism/mcp_session {
  focus mcp_session
  project mcp_session
  split mcp_session
  shift mcp_session
  settle mcp_session
}

# ============================================================
# §2 The MCP session record — three surfaces specialised
# ============================================================

# === mcp_session — the session-state-machine record ===
#
# Inherits the gen_prism three-surface shape from the family root,
# specialised for MCP:
#
#   identity  — session_uuid: uuid_spectral. ACTIVE 48 bits route
#               the session in the substrate's spectral manifold;
#               DARK 80 bits identify it content-addressably for
#               session ref lookup and cross-restart persistence.
#   state     — shard_ref pointing at the head crystal of the
#               accumulated @spec inside @mirror/store. Resolution
#               through @mirror/store.read. State changes ARE
#               settles into a new shard (lattice ascent per
#               [[architecture-shard-as-crdt]]).
#   parent    — supervisor gen_prism's uuid_spectral. The parent
#               is the MCP-session supervisor (a
#               @spectral/supervisor specialisation; forward-
#               promised at `shards/spectral/supervisor.mirror`);
#               owns restart-strategy on daemon crash.
#
# The session ref (`refs/gen_prism/mcp/<session-uuid>`) is not a
# record field; it is a store-side ref that names this record by
# its `session_uuid` identity. The ref advances by CAS as the
# session ticks; the record's `state` field IS the current head
# crystal-oid the ref resolves to.
type mcp_session = {
  session_uuid: uuid_spectral,
  state:        shard_ref,
  parent:       uuid_spectral,
}

# ============================================================
# §3 The tick action — read head, apply mq, write, CAS-advance
# ============================================================

# === tick — the session's mutation primitive ===
#
# Reads the session's head crystal from
# `refs/gen_prism/mcp/<session-uuid>`, applies an mq query (the
# decoded JSON-RPC request), writes the resulting new crystal to
# @mirror/store, and CAS-advances the ref from the old head oid
# to the new head oid.
#
# Per collapse spec §3.6 tick semantics:
#
#   1. READ. Resolve `refs/gen_prism/mcp/<session-uuid>` to the
#      head crystal-oid; read the crystal content as the input
#      @spec.
#   2. APPLY. Decode the JSON-RPC request as an mq query per
#      `boot/std/code/mq.mirror`; apply the query against the
#      input @spec; produce the output @spec + JSON-RPC response
#      payload.
#   3. WRITE. Content-address the output @spec; write the crystal
#      to @mirror/store; receive back the new crystal-oid.
#   4. CAS-ADVANCE. Compare-and-swap the ref from old-head-oid to
#      new-head-oid. On success, the session's head advances by
#      one lattice element (per [[architecture-shard-as-crdt]])
#      and the response is emitted. On conflict (another concurrent
#      tick advanced the ref first), retry from step 1.
#
# The tick body stays obligation-blocked (`\`): the realisation
# lands as Rust wiring at a follow-on M1 tick (per collapse spec
# §10.1). This tick declares the substrate-decl vocabulary the
# wiring consumes.
#
# The tick IS this species's specialisation of the family-root's
# `settle @ runtime` — measurement collapse driving pending au
# into a new shard through the property chain. At MCP altitude,
# each JSON-RPC request drives one tick; the session's state
# surface advances by one lattice element per request; the
# accumulated @spec grows monotonically until settle_on ratifies.
tick(s: mcp_session, request: ref) -> mcp_session { \ }

# ============================================================
# §4 The read-head action — resolve the session's head crystal
# ============================================================

# === read_head — resolve the session's current head crystal ===
#
# Given a session_uuid, resolve `refs/gen_prism/mcp/<session-uuid>`
# to the current head crystal-oid and read the crystal content.
# This IS step 1 of the tick, extracted as a first-class action
# because:
#
#   - read-only queries dispatch here without needing to advance
#     the ref (many MCP calls are pure reads);
#   - session-resume-after-daemon-restart reads through this
#     action to reconstruct the pre-restart session state;
#   - replay reads any ancestor crystal in the query trajectory
#     through this action with a different oid.
#
# Composes with @mirror/store's read primitive at the ref-lookup
# altitude. Body obligation-blocked (`\`).
read_head(session_uuid: uuid_spectral) -> shard_ref { \ }

# ============================================================
# §5 The advance-ref action — CAS the session ref
# ============================================================

# === advance_ref — CAS-advance the session ref ===
#
# The CAS (compare-and-swap) primitive: advance
# `refs/gen_prism/mcp/<session-uuid>` from `old_head` to
# `new_head` atomically. Returns `pass` if the ref currently
# equals `old_head` and the advance succeeded; `failure` if the
# ref has been advanced by another tick (contention; caller
# retries from step 1 of the tick).
#
# The advance-by-CAS semantic IS the substrate's session-mutation
# primitive per collapse spec §3.6 and per git-ref prior art
# (Torvalds 2005; `git update-ref --create-reflog <ref> <new>
# <old>`). Contention resolves at the ref-advance edge; no
# in-process locking is required because @mirror/store carries
# the atomicity at the git-backed floor.
#
# Body obligation-blocked (`\`); the realisation delegates to
# @mirror/store's ref-advance primitive when the Rust wiring
# lands.
advance_ref(
  session_uuid: uuid_spectral,
  old_head:     shard_ref,
  new_head:     shard_ref,
) -> verdict { \ }

# ============================================================
# §6 The out clauses
# ============================================================

out @spectral/gen_prism/mcp_session
out mcp_session
out tick
out read_head
out advance_ref
